Bundled icons
=============

`hicolor/symbolic/apps/scriptura-*.svg` are this app's own icon set. Most are
copied unchanged from the GNOME Adwaita icon theme and renamed with a
`scriptura-` prefix; a handful were drawn for this app.

Why they are copied rather than looked up by their usual names: an icon name
like `starred-symbolic` resolves out of whatever icon theme the user happens
to run, so the same button is flat line art on one desktop and a coloured
cartoon on another. A name nothing else claims always resolves to ours, on
every desktop and across icon-theme releases. The app pins its icon theme as
well (see `_pin_icon_theme` in main.py) — that covers GTK's own lookups, which
renaming cannot reach — but the copies are what make the app's own iconography
independent of both the user's theme and of Adwaita's future renamings.

Window controls are deliberately NOT bundled. `window-close-symbolic` and its
siblings stay with the desktop, so the button that closes this window is the
one that closes every other window on the user's screen.

